<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch May cash retail sales rise 6.3 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Dutch May cash retail sales rise 6.3 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch retail sales rose 6.3 percent in cash terms in May compared with May 1996, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.</p>
<p>In volume terms May retail sales were 5.3 percent higher than in May 1996, the CBS added.  </p>
<p>DUTCH RETAIL SALES		     May 97   April 97     May 96</p>
<p> Pct change cash yr/yr		   6.3	 3.2	   6.3</p>
<p>     index (base 1994)		   118	 106	   111</p>
<p> Pct change prices yr/yr		 1.0	 0.0	   0.0</p>
<p>     index (base 1994)		   102	 101	   101</p>
<p> Pct change volume yr/yr		 5.3	 3.2	   6.3</p>
<p>     index (base 1994)		   116	 105	   110</p>
<p> DUTCH RETAIL SALES IN DETAIL	 May 97    April 97</p>
<p>					     (pct changes yr/yr)</p>
<p> Food cash				   6.2	  3.0</p>
<p> Food prices				 1.9	  0.0</p>
<p> Food volume				 4.2	  3.0</p>
<p> Durable goods &amp; non-food cash	 7.0	  3.7</p>
<p> Durable goods &amp; non-food prices     0.4	  0.0</p>
<p> Durable goods &amp; non-food volume     6.6	  3.7</p>
<p>NOTES - The CBS noted that May 1997 had one Wednesday less and one Saturday more than May 1996. It said that if the figures were adjusted to eliminate the effect of this difference in shopping days, then total May cash retail sales would show a rise of some 3.5 percent compared with the same month of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
